 "@graph": [
  {
   "@id": "chapter/01",
   "@type": "Chapter",
   "n": 1,
   "label": "01. The tether",
   "title": "The tether",
   "code": "TH",
   "say": "X3D can be held to account because a program can name exactly what is wrong with a file, a second program can show what the file draws, and the record of both checks can travel inside the file; this holds for structure and behaviour, while appearance and intent still need a renderer and a person.",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.docs/blob/ff0565e5a248ca391d68527716a58a821f25d152/docs/learn/01-the-tether.md",
   "file": "docs/learn/01-the-tether.md",
   "grade": [
    "grade/L"
   ],
   "citesPin": [
    "pin/x3d.docs@f172f67",
    "pin/x3d.loom@162ab18",
    "pin/x3d_mcp@535fdac",
    "pin/x3d_mcp@b4efcd3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "chapter/02",
   "@type": "Chapter",
   "n": 2,
   "label": "02. The Loom laws",
   "title": "The Loom laws",
   "code": "LAW",
   "say": "the Loom is 44 numbered laws and 160 numbered failure modes, each paid for by a recorded failure; this chapter indexes them by number so you can find the law that forbids a mistake, the incident that created it, and the check that catches it. [L] (the counts are [C], parsed from the file)",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.docs/blob/ff0565e5a248ca391d68527716a58a821f25d152/docs/learn/02-loom-laws.md",
   "file": "docs/learn/02-loom-laws.md",
   "requires": [
    "chapter/01"
   ],
   "citesPin": [
    "pin/x3d.docs@f172f67",
    "pin/x3d.loom@0244784",
    "pin/x3d.loom@162ab18",
    "pin/x3d.loom@babba96"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "chapter/03",
   "@type": "Chapter",
   "n": 3,
   "label": "03. The validator and the gates",
   "title": "The validator and the gates",
   "code": "VAL",
   "say": "A validator is a ladder, not a verdict: every rung names what it checked, the rungs below the renderer cannot see \"looks right\", and a verdict without a commit and a schema version is a rumour.",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.docs/blob/ff0565e5a248ca391d68527716a58a821f25d152/docs/learn/03-validator-and-gates.md",
   "file": "docs/learn/03-validator-and-gates.md",
   "grade": [
    "grade/C"
   ],
   "requires": [
    "chapter/01",
    "chapter/02"
   ],
   "citesPin": [
    "pin/x3d-blender-io@ab99988",
    "pin/x3d.docs@f172f67",
    "pin/x3d.loom@162ab18",
    "pin/x3d_mcp@74da0ec",
    "pin/x3d_mcp@b4efcd3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "chapter/04",
   "@type": "Chapter",
   "n": 4,
   "label": "04. x3d_mcp as the agent interface",
   "title": "x3d_mcp as the agent interface",
   "code": "MCP",
   "say": "x3d_mcp gives a model 53 callable tools whose answers are small, structured and checkable, tells it the canonical path on connect, and keeps big documents and hostile queries out of its context with guards that live in the tool, not in the prompt.",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.docs/blob/ff0565e5a248ca391d68527716a58a821f25d152/docs/learn/04-mcp-for-agents.md",
   "file": "docs/learn/04-mcp-for-agents.md",
   "grade": [
    "grade/C"
   ],
   "requires": [
    "chapter/01",
    "chapter/03"
   ],
   "citesPin": [
    "pin/x3d.docs@f172f67",
    "pin/x3d_mcp@74da0ec",
    "pin/x3d_mcp@b4efcd3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "chapter/05",
   "@type": "Chapter",
   "n": 5,
   "label": "05. The semantic layer: RDF, OWL, SPARQL, SHACL on X3D",
   "title": "The semantic layer: RDF, OWL, SPARQL, SHACL on X3D",
   "code": "SEM",
   "say": "An X3D scene can be turned into a graph of facts, questioned with SPARQL, held to SHACL shapes and (carefully) reasoned over, but the ontology only proposes, the shapes dispose and the validators gate; every result names a node, a check id and an instrument.",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.docs/blob/ff0565e5a248ca391d68527716a58a821f25d152/docs/learn/05-semantic-layer.md",
   "file": "docs/learn/05-semantic-layer.md",
   "grade": [
    "grade/C"
   ],
   "requires": [
    "chapter/01",
    "chapter/03"
   ],
   "citesPin": [
    "pin/x3d.demo@d10b457",
    "pin/x3d.docs@f172f67",
    "pin/x3d_mcp@13121b6",
    "pin/x3d_mcp@b4efcd3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "chapter/06",
   "@type": "Chapter",
   "n": 6,
   "label": "06. X_ITE, the reference renderer",
   "title": "X_ITE, the reference renderer",
   "code": "XIT",
   "say": "X_ITE is the second program that tells you what a scene draws and what its events do, and it is a good oracle only when you name its patch, its browser and its options, drive it with guarded code, and remember that it is a renderer with its own extensions, not a validator.",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.docs/blob/ff0565e5a248ca391d68527716a58a821f25d152/docs/learn/06-xite-the-oracle.md",
   "file": "docs/learn/06-xite-the-oracle.md",
   "grade": [
    "grade/C"
   ],
   "requires": [
    "chapter/01",
    "chapter/03"
   ],
   "citesPin": [
    "pin/x3d.demo@d10b457",
    "pin/x3d.docs@f172f67",
    "pin/x3d.loom@162ab18",
    "pin/x3d.xray@8fa6845",
    "pin/x3d_mcp@b4efcd3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "chapter/07",
   "@type": "Chapter",
   "n": 7,
   "label": "07. x3d.xray, the X-ray method",
   "title": "x3d.xray, the X-ray method",
   "code": "XRY",
   "say": "x3d.xray turns the git history of a family of repositories into one X3D scene whose every number is computed by code, graded by checks declared before the data is read, and re-derived by a second reader; on a repository too thin to grade, its honest output is \"not run\".",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.docs/blob/ff0565e5a248ca391d68527716a58a821f25d152/docs/learn/07-xray.md",
   "file": "docs/learn/07-xray.md",
   "grade": [
    "grade/C"
   ],
   "requires": [
    "chapter/01",
    "chapter/03",
    "chapter/06"
   ],
   "citesPin": [
    "pin/x3d.castle@d70e00c",
    "pin/x3d.xray@8fa6845",
    "pin/x3d_mcp@b4efcd3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "chapter/08",
   "@type": "Chapter",
   "n": 8,
   "label": "08. The Babylon bridge",
   "title": "The Babylon bridge",
   "code": "BAB",
   "say": "one X3D file is the master, our own reader runs its events, and Babylon on WebGPU only paints the result; every picture is a claim against X_ITE on a named rig, every fallback says so on screen, and nothing about speed has been measured.",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.docs/blob/ff0565e5a248ca391d68527716a58a821f25d152/docs/learn/08-babylon-bridge.md",
   "file": "docs/learn/08-babylon-bridge.md",
   "grade": [
    "grade/C"
   ],
   "requires": [
    "chapter/01",
    "chapter/02",
    "chapter/06"
   ],
   "citesPin": [
    "pin/x3d.demo@d10b457",
    "pin/x3d.docs@f172f67",
    "pin/x3d.loom@108a282",
    "pin/x3d.loom@1192dd4",
    "pin/x3d.loom@162ab18",
    "pin/x3d.loom@38530ab",
    "pin/x3d.loom@4887a98",
    "pin/x3d.loom@60824ce",
    "pin/x3d.loom@72a4bca",
    "pin/x3d.loom@80388ce",
    "pin/x3d.loom@8a1e769",
    "pin/x3d.loom@95eda37",
