   "@id": "drill/D-BAB-3",
   "@type": "Drill",
   "label": "D-BAB-3 Break a shader key, then predict which half moves",
   "title": "Break a shader key, then predict which half moves",
   "level": "L3",
   "task": "Compute the keys of the five ComposedShaders in `x3d.webgpu/demo/collider.x3d` with an independent implementation and compare them with the `key:` fields in `collider-v2.html`. Then (a) add runs of spaces inside `flashShader2`'s fragment and (b) change `u_phase * 12.0` to `u_phase * 12.5`; predict both keys first.",
   "verify": "```python import re, sys, urllib.parse from lxml import etree def fnv(s): h = 0x811c9dc5 for c in s: h = ((h ^ ord(c)) * 0x01000193) & 0xffffffff return '%08x' % h n = lambda s: re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', s).strip() def src(u): b = re.match(r'\\s*\"?(data:[^\"]*)\"?\\s*$', u, re.S).group(1).split(',', 1)[1] return urllib.parse.unquote(b) if re.search(r'%[0-9a-fA-F]{2}', b) else b for cs in etree.parse(sys.argv[1]).iter('ComposedShader'): if cs.get('DEF'): # USE copies carry no parts p = {x.get('type').upper(): src(x.get('url')) for x in cs.iter('ShaderPart')} print(cs.get('DEF'), fnv(n(p['VERTEX'])) + '-' + fnv(n(p['FRAGMENT']))) ```",
   "answer": "the five keys equal the table in section 9. (a) leaves `1bc84a9f-b6fcc411` unchanged; (b) gives `1bc84a9f-bd1839be`: only the fragment half moves and the page would miss the port and fall back.",
   "checkedText": "2026-11-14 `x3d.loom@162ab18`, Python 3 with lxml, scratch copies of the scene",
   "status": "ran",
