   "@id": "drill/D-JEV-2",
   "@type": "Drill",
   "label": "D-JEV-2 A bar from a lower bound",
   "title": "A bar from a lower bound",
   "level": "L2",
   "task": "For 90 and for 98 correct answers out of 100 in one probability bin, compute the Wilson 95% lower bound and say whether either clears a 0.85 target.",
   "verify": "the function below. ```python import math def wilson_lo(k, n, z=1.96): ph = k / n; d = 1 + z*z/n; c = ph + z*z/(2*n) h = z * math.sqrt(ph*(1-ph)/n + z*z/(4*n*n)) return (c - h) / d for k in (90, 98): print(k, round(wilson_lo(k, 100), 3), wilson_lo(k, 100) >= 0.85) ```",
   "answer": "90 gives 0.826 (does not clear); 98 gives 0.93 (clears). A point precision of 0.90 would have set the bar; the lower bound refuses it.",
   "checkedText": "2026-11-16 Python 3.13.18",
   "status": "ran",
   "checkedOn": "2026-11-16",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.docs/blob/ff0565e5a248ca391d68527716a58a821f25d152/docs/learn/22-typed-judgments-jev.md?plain=1#L274",
