   "@id": "drill/D-JEV-7",
   "@type": "Drill",
   "label": "D-JEV-7 The dead branch",
   "title": "The dead branch",
   "level": "L2",
   "task": "The behaviour slice counted timers with the chain below. Run it over three tags and say what the old order reports for a `TimeSensor`, then reorder it.",
   "verify": "the script below. ```python def count(tags, fixed): c = {\"timers\": 0, \"interpolators\": 0, \"sensors\": 0} for t in tags: if t.endswith(\"Interpolator\"): c[\"interpolators\"] += 1 elif fixed and t == \"TimeSensor\": c[\"timers\"] += 1; c[\"sensors\"] += 1 elif t.endswith(\"Sensor\"): c[\"sensors\"] += 1 elif t == \"TimeSensor\": c[\"timers\"] += 1 # unreachable in the old order return c for fixed in (False, True): print(fixed, count([\"TimeSensor\", \"Transform\", \"TouchSensor\"], fixed)) ```",
   "answer": "the old order prints `timers: 0` (the `TimeSensor` is caught by the generic `Sensor` test first); the fixed order prints `timers: 1`. \"Is animated\" is a timer or an interpolator, so the old code answers no for a scene animated only by a timer.",
   "checkedText": "2026-11-17 Python 3.13.18",
