   "@id": "drill/D-PHY-1",
   "@type": "Drill",
   "label": "D-PHY-1 Symplectic against explicit Euler on a pendulum",
   "title": "Symplectic against explicit Euler on a pendulum",
   "level": "L2",
   "task": "Integrate a pendulum (L = 1, theta0 = 1 rad, h = 0.01, T = 100 s) with explicit Euler and with symplectic Euler. Report final and maximum relative energy change `(E - E0)/E0`.",
   "verify": "```python def pend(method, h, T, th0=1.0, L=1.0): th, w = th0, 0.0 E = lambda th, w: 0.5*L*L*w*w + g*L*(1-math.cos(th)) E0 = E(th, w); Es = [] for _ in range(int(round(T/h))): if method == 'explicit': a = -g/L*math.sin(th); th, w = th + h*w, w + h*a else: w += h*(-g/L*math.sin(th)); th += h*w Es.append(E(th, w)) return E0, np.array(Es) for m in ('explicit', 'symplectic'): E0, Es = pend(m, 0.01, 100) print(m, (Es[-1]-E0)/E0, np.max(abs(Es-E0))/E0) ```",
   "answer": "explicit: final +10.89, max 11.01 (energy has grown elevenfold). Symplectic: final +0.0002, max 0.0150 (bounded oscillation around the shadow energy).",
   "checkedText": "`2026-11-14 python3 -I numpy 2.5.3`: explicit 10.8933 and 11.0130, symplectic 0.0002 and 0.0150.",
   "status": "ran",
   "checkedOn": "2026-11-14",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.docs/blob/ff0565e5a248ca391d68527716a58a821f25d152/docs/learn/13-physics.md?plain=1#L456",
