  {
   "@id": "drill/D-PHY-6",
   "@type": "Drill",
   "label": "D-PHY-6 The CFL limit is a stability limit, not \"outrunning a cell\"",
   "title": "The CFL limit is a stability limit, not \"outrunning a cell\"",
   "level": "L3",
   "task": "Run the 2D wave equation `v += (c dt/dx)^2 * laplacian(u); u += v` (symplectic Euler, 5-point Laplacian, fixed boundaries) on a 28 x 28 grid with a 1e-3 random start, 400 steps, at c dt/dx = 0.60, 0.70, 0.7071, 0.72, 0.80. Then bisect the limit and explain it with the largest Laplacian eigenvalue.",
   "verify": "```python def wave(cfl, N=28, steps=400): u = np.zeros((N, N)); vv = np.zeros((N, N)); rng = np.random.default_rng(1) u[1:-1, 1:-1] = rng.normal(size=(N-2, N-2))*1e-3; k = cfl*cfl for _ in range(steps): lap = np.zeros_like(u) lap[1:-1, 1:-1] = u[2:, 1:-1]+u[:-2, 1:-1]+u[1:-1, 2:]+u[1:-1, :-2]-4*u[1:-1, 1:-1] vv += k*lap; u += vv; u[0] = u[-1] = 0; u[:, 0] = u[:, -1] = 0 return np.abs(u).max() for c in (0.6, 0.70, 0.7071, 0.72, 0.8): print(c, wave(c)) ```",
   "answer": "at 0.60, 0.70 and 0.7071 the amplitude stays near 1e-3 to 5e-3; at 0.72 it is 1.2e59 and at 0.80 4.4e170. Stability needs `c^2 dt^2 lambda_max <= 4`; for the 5-point Laplacian lambda_max/dx^2 tends to 8 in two dimensions, giving `c dt/dx <= 1/sqrt(2) = 0.7071` (0.7082 on the finite 28 x 28 grid per the review's bisection, because the finite grid's largest eigenvalue is a bit under 8). The wave speed in cells per step (0.72) is under one, so \"outrunning a cell\" cannot be the cause. The bisection to 0.7082 was **not** run here.",
   "checkedText": "`2026-11-14 python3 -I numpy 2.5.3`: 0.6 -> 2.69e-03; 0.70 -> 3.42e-03; 0.7071 -> 4.65e-03; 0.72 -> 1.18e+59; 0.80 -> 4.40e+170. Bisection not run.",
   "status": "ran",
   "checkedOn": "2026-11-14",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.docs/blob/ff0565e5a248ca391d68527716a58a821f25d152/docs/learn/13-physics.md?plain=1#L553",
