   "verify": "```python from PIL import Image; from flip_score import score im = Image.open(\"results/strips/e2-cornell-box.webp\").convert(\"RGB\") for i, n in enumerate(\"xcrp\"): im.crop((320 * i, 0, 320 * i + 320, 240)).save(f\"/tmp/{n}.png\") print(score(\"/tmp/x.png\", \"/tmp/p.png\", [0, 0, 0])) ```",
   "answer": "0.264. The strip is lossy webp (quality 88), so the value moves by about 0.001 from 0.265 measured on the PNGs; it is a reproduction check, not a new measurement.",
