   "@type": "FailureMode",
   "n": 66,
   "label": "Failure mode 66",
   "failure": "A negative control that cannot fail proves nothing: at a mirror-symmetric view (an edge-on disk) the vertically flipped capture still correlated 0.981, so the witness could not see an orientation error there",
   "fix": "Keep the control required to fail, and choose evidence views that make it bite (asymmetric framing); never relax the control to get a pass",
