   "@id": "fm/76",
   "@type": "FailureMode",
   "n": 76,
   "label": "Failure mode 76",
   "failure": "Limits declared from an exploration that skipped the hardest cases: the 3D normalization limit was measured on 1s, 2p, 3d, 4f, 5g, and the first build went red on 3s and the superposition (the s-state cusp at the nucleus, coarsely sampled in a large box)",
   "fix": "Explore the worst case before declaring a limit; when a red is resolution, show it by refinement (observed order, extrapolated value), then measure the cause on a finer check grid with the same limit and report the display-grid number; keep the red run in history",
   "sourceText": "[Electron Cloud first build, 4 Nov; C]",
