   ],
   "fixedByLaw": [
    "law/36"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "fm/94",
   "@type": "FailureMode",
   "n": 94,
   "label": "Failure mode 94",
   "failure": "The X_ITE freeze (failure mode 88) on a second delivery, one not built under the Loom: one exception from the slide show's conductor stopped the piece for good. The clock advanced 1.5 s in 1.5 s before the throw and 0 s in 2 s after; the scene's TimeSensor stopped; a callback added afterwards was never called; seeking moved the playhead, which then stood still. The delivered feature checks and a clean console never exercise this path, and the earlier director page has the same callback",
   "fix": "A guard in both pages, as a fold-back patch (`runs/mashtots2-20261105/foldback/stage-onframe-guard.patch`), applied to the demo copy (`projects/mashtots-slideshow`) on 5 Nov at the user's word; and committed to the source repo (`~/Projects/x3d/work/mashtots-standalones/slideshow`, eae4235). With it, the clock advanced 2.0 s in 2.0 s past the same throw, the feature checks pass 150 of 150, and page traps pass. The resilience probe belongs in every X_ITE page's evidence, not only in the Loom's own studies",
   "sourceText": "[MASH2; C (L3): headless Chromium through Playwright, X_ITE 16.5.1]",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L486",
   "line": 486,
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ],
   "citesSource": [
    "source/MASH2"
   ],
   "inClass": [
    "class/K5"
   ],
   "mentions": [
    "fm/88"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "fm/95",
   "@type": "FailureMode",
   "n": 95,
   "label": "Failure mode 95",
   "failure": "Widening a witness's reading made a false positive: the first inline-script run flagged a module script's top-level let frames as shadowing window.frames, but a module's top-level names never reach window (the page passes 150 of 150 checks)",
   "fix": "The window-name rule skips module code (`type=\"module\"`, and .js files with a top-level import or export), with a two-sided form for each. Re-run the change on the six studies and both deliveries before trusting it (law 8)",
   "sourceText": "[this repository, 5 Nov; C]",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L487",
