   "@id": "fm/99",
   "@type": "FailureMode",
   "n": 99,
   "label": "Failure mode 99",
   "failure": "Provenance that lives in .git did not travel: the report and README rest provenance on local commits (\"the first commit is the verbatim copy; git diff shows every change\"), and neither zip contains .git. The repos happen to be on this Mac (~/Projects/x3d/work/mashtots-standalones/): they carry the named commits, and their working trees match the delivery file for file, logs aside (slide show: 205 tracked files, git diff d148f8f HEAD = 31 files, +1245 −16). A receiver anywhere else could not check it",
   "fix": "Ship the diff or a git bundle with the delivery. The receiver checks every provenance claim against what arrived and says where the check was possible. My first reading called the claim uncheckable before looking for the repos (law 26)",
   "sourceText": "[MASH2; C, checked here against the local repos]",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L491",
