  {
   "@id": "law/26",
   "@type": "Law",
   "n": 26,
   "label": "Law 26: Suspect the witness first",
   "headline": "Suspect the witness first",
   "text": "A red, or a surprise, is first a question about what the witness measured. The same value across unrelated inputs, or no change when its supposed cause changes, means it measures something else",
   "forbids": "Debugging the subject before the instrument",
   "paidForByText": "Kerr 2's 'GPU error' was a capture of the wrong view; the Turing Garden's quantization check returned 0.31 cells in every case at 8 and 16 bits (C, failure modes 64, 70)",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L116",
   "line": 116,
   "evidenceText": "a wrong-view capture read as a GPU bug; a check returned 0.31 cells in every case (fm 64, 70, src C)",
   "violation": "debugging the subject before the instrument",
