   "@id": "law/38",
   "@type": "Law",
   "n": 38,
   "label": "Law 38: One master, many renderers",
   "headline": "One master, many renderers",
   "text": "A second renderer reads the validated X3D itself, never a converted copy. Parity between renderers is the same sha256, the reader's coverage manifest (every node and ROUTE read, or named as skipped) and a shape witness per beat (a mask's IoU); never a pixel hash across renderers",
   "forbids": "A second renderer fed from an export that can drift from the master; renderer-only geometry",
   "paidForByText": "Both rebuilds drew from converted copies: one 50 % larger than the gzipped X3D, one carrying geometry and a moon the scene did not hold and a miswired reveal. The merged build reads 48 of 48 ROUTEs from the X3D, cloth mask IoU 0.976 to 0.992 at 10 beats (C, failure modes 115, 123; [RB1])",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L128",
   "line": 128,
   "evidenceText": "both rebuilds drew from converted copies; merged build reads 48 of 48 ROUTEs, cloth mask IoU 0.976 to 0.992 (fm 115, 123)",
   "violation": "a second renderer fed from a drifting export; a pixel hash across renderers",
   "checkText": "process: same sha256, a coverage manifest, a shape witness per beat",
   "checkKind": "process",
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ],
   "evidenceGrade": [
    "grade/C"
   ],
   "citesSource": [
    "source/RB1"
   ],
   "inTheme": [
    "theme/I"
   ],
   "paidForBy": [
    "fm/115",
    "fm/123"
   ]
  },
