   "@id": "law/39",
   "@type": "Law",
   "n": 39,
   "label": "Law 39: A look may add, never assert",
   "headline": "A look may add, never assert",
   "text": "Decoration, generated fill and display exaggeration are labelled where they are seen and travel with the pixels (an ART mark burned into exports and filenames, a 1× switch next to any exaggeration). A defect is fixed at its source, not hidden by the tone curve",
   "forbids": "Generated detail leaving the page unlabelled; clipping hidden by tone mapping",
   "paidForByText": "The face-relief rebuild burned ART into every generated-fill export and added a source-1× depth switch (adopted, L); the tomb's clipping went 88.4 % to 0 % by changing the light values, not the tone curve (C, X_ITE 16.5.1, failure mode 114; [RB1], [RB2])",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L129",
