  {
   "@id": "law/41",
   "@type": "Law",
   "n": 41,
   "label": "Law 41: A replaced engine is shown off, in every host that has it, and its leaks are listed",
   "headline": "A replaced engine is shown off, in every host that has it, and its leaks are listed",
   "text": "When page code takes over from a runtime's own implementation (here a physics engine), the record shows the old one stepping nothing in each host, that writes made while it is disabled stick, that re-enabling resumes from them, and every step it took before the switch",
   "forbids": "Assuming \"disabled\" means off; a takeover proved in one browser",
   "paidForByText": "X_ITE 16.7's Bullet stepped once after `loadURL()` resolved (y 0.32 to 0.319974 to 0.319989); loading with `createX3DFromURL`, disabling, then `replaceWorld` leaks none, shown in Chromium 145, Firefox 146 and WebKit 26 (C, failure mode 127; [PXB])",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L131",
   "line": 131,
   "evidenceText": "X_ITE's Bullet stepped once after `loadURL()` (y 0.32 to 0.319974, fm 127)",
   "violation": "taking \"disabled\" for \"off\"",
   "checkText": "code: `PHYS_TAKEOVER_UNPROVEN`",
   "checkKind": "code",
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ],
   "evidenceGrade": [
    "grade/C"
   ],
   "citesSource": [
    "source/PXB"
   ],
   "inTheme": [
    "theme/J"
   ],
   "paidForBy": [
    "fm/127"
   ],
   "caughtBy": [
    "diag/PHYS_TAKEOVER_UNPROVEN"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "law/42",
   "@type": "Law",
   "n": 42,
   "label": "Law 42: Determinism is claimed per step and per host",
   "headline": "Determinism is claimed per step and per host",
   "text": "A simulation run records a hash of every step's state and is replayed in each host it names, Node included; the first step that differs is reported. A claim in one host is not a claim in another, and a claim on one machine is not a claim on a second",
   "forbids": "A final-state hash alone; \"deterministic\" said of a run replayed in one place; a hash that leaves out state",
   "paidForByText": "PhysX 5.12 replayed 1918 steps recorded in Chromium and 969 recorded in Firefox with 0 differing hashes in Chromium, Firefox, WebKit and Node; across machines was not run (C, failure modes 128, 129; [PXB]). The play witness (6 Nov) already compared a final-state hash on one JavaScript engine",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L132",
   "line": 132,
   "evidenceText": "1918 steps recorded in Chromium, 969 in Firefox, 0 differing hashes in 4 hosts (fm 128, 129; one machine)",
   "violation": "a final-state hash; a claim from one place",
   "checkText": "code: `PHYS_HASH_DRIFT`, `PHYS_REPLAY_MISSING`, `PHYS_REPLAY_STEPS`, `PHYS_ENGINE_DRIFT`, `PHYS_TRACE_TAMPERED`",
   "checkKind": "code",
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ],
   "evidenceGrade": [
    "grade/C"
   ],
   "citesSource": [
    "source/PXB"
   ],
   "inTheme": [
    "theme/J"
   ],
   "paidForBy": [
    "fm/128",
    "fm/129"
   ],
   "caughtBy": [
    "diag/PHYS_ENGINE_DRIFT",
    "diag/PHYS_HASH_DRIFT",
    "diag/PHYS_REPLAY_MISSING",
    "diag/PHYS_REPLAY_STEPS",
    "diag/PHYS_TRACE_TAMPERED"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "law/43",
   "@type": "Law",
   "n": 43,
   "label": "Law 43: A tolerance is written before the run; an excursion is a waiver, not a pass",
   "headline": "A tolerance is written before the run; an excursion is a waiver, not a pass",
   "text": "Limits are declared first and may not be widened afterwards. A measure beyond its limit is recorded as an accepted failure with its owner, date, reason and its own numbers; the profile caps how many; a receipt lists them. A self-check that misses its closed form is logged with its probable cause and is never tuned to fit. *Scope: physics profiles only, for now (13 Nov decision); if it proves wrong it is marked a false positive in this table, not deleted*",
   "forbids": "Loosening a threshold to turn red green; a green label on a failing number; a failure with no name on it",
   "paidForByText": "3 of 33 browser smoke tests failed under load (Galton 220 and 223 of 240 beads against 225; a music box turn 15 of 18 pegs) and the owner accepted them: three waivers under the PhysX profile's cap of three. A ragdoll's limit overshoot reached 0.43 rad against 0.2, and its Gravitron check missed its closed form by 34 % (2.97 against 2.22 rad/s): logged, not tuned (C, failure modes 133, 137; [PXB])",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L133",
   "line": 133,
   "evidenceText": "3 of 33 smoke tests failed under load and were accepted as 3 waivers; ragdoll overshoot 0.43 against 0.2 rad (fm 133, 137)",
   "violation": "loosening a threshold to turn red green",
   "checkText": "code: `PHYS_LIMIT_WIDENED`, `PHYS_FALSE_GREEN`, `PHYS_WAIVER_INCOMPLETE`, `PHYS_WAIVERS_OVER_CAP`; cap 3 passes and cap 0 fails on the real records (re-run, [C])",
   "checkKind": "code",
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ],
   "evidenceGrade": [
    "grade/C"
   ],
   "citesSource": [
    "source/PXB"
   ],
   "inTheme": [
    "theme/J"
   ],
   "paidForBy": [
    "fm/133",
    "fm/137"
   ],
   "caughtBy": [
    "diag/PHYS_FALSE_GREEN",
    "diag/PHYS_LIMIT_WIDENED",
    "diag/PHYS_WAIVERS_OVER_CAP",
    "diag/PHYS_WAIVER_INCOMPLETE"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "law/44",
   "@type": "Law",
   "n": 44,
   "label": "Law 44: A check is shown able to fail, and a number is not Confirmed until a second reader has tried to break it",
   "headline": "A check is shown able to fail, and a number is not Confirmed until a second reader has tried to break it",
   "text": "Every reference ships with a wrong implementation it must reject (a control that fails when the code is right is a bug in the control too); a mutation control that changes nothing is counted as missing; a limit file is committed before the run and the runner refuses to start if it differs from its commit; a number the author reads is graded Likely until someone who did not write it has recomputed it. *Scope: physics profiles first, like law 43*",
   "forbids": "A check that passes for a wrong implementation; a quantity read after the step that enforces it; a limit that cannot be shown to precede the run; a self-graded Confirmed",
   "paidForByText": "The Ten Minute Physics ports' own review (13 Nov): 4 reviewers recomputed v1 to v4, 125 claims checked, 25 negative findings survived a second skeptical agent, 0 false alarms. The kinetic-energy check read 1.33e-15 with the buggy collision rule, 2.0e-15 with the fixed one and 0 with no collisions. In batch 6, 2 of 11 mutation controls scaled a limit of 0 and changed nothing (C, failure modes 148 to 160; PHYSICS-PLAYBOOK patterns 11 to 19)",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L134",
   "line": 134,
   "evidenceText": "the energy check read 1.33e-15 with the buggy rule, 2.0e-15 fixed, 0 with no collisions (fm 148); 125 claims, 25 negative findings survived (src C)",
   "violation": "a self-graded Confirmed; a mutation control that changes nothing (fm 157: 2 of 11)",
   "checkText": "code: `PHYS_CONTROL_SURVIVED`; 14 of 14 mutations of the real record caught (re-run, [C]); limits-commit check is not in the kit",
   "checkKind": "code",
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ],
   "evidenceGrade": [
    "grade/C"
   ],
   "inTheme": [
    "theme/B"
   ],
   "paidForBy": [
    "fm/148",
    "fm/149",
