   "@id": "question/1",
   "@type": "OpenQuestion",
   "n": 1,
   "label": "Open question 1: Promote the five fold-back patches?",
   "headline": "Promote the five fold-back patches?",
   "text": "Four pass loom foldback here. Applying them to x3d.onto, the fork or x3d.ML is a PR into your repos, so it waits for your word, and those repos are not checked out on this Mac. Which first? Break-the-Loom's own table suggests Traps and shared acceptance code [BREAK].",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L588",
   "line": 588,
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "question/10",
