  {
   "@id": "question/12",
   "@type": "OpenQuestion",
   "n": 12,
   "label": "Open question 12: Create hagopjay/x3d.STEM",
   "headline": "Create hagopjay/x3d.STEM",
   "text": "(this Mac's account cannot create repos under hagopjay); then the Scientific Loom, sci.py, the profile and X3D-STEM.md can move there by PR.",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L599",
   "line": 599,
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "question/13",
   "@type": "OpenQuestion",
   "n": 13,
   "label": "Open question 13: Send the hardening patch to the Scientific Loom's next pass?",
   "headline": "Send the hardening patch to the Scientific Loom's next pass?",
   "text": "It fixes the component declarations and four of the seven assert gates; candidate binding for browser evidence still needs their harness.",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L600",
   "line": 600,
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "question/14",
   "@type": "OpenQuestion",
   "n": 14,
   "label": "Open question 14: Exclude the Loom's evidence directory by path, not by name?",
   "headline": "Exclude the Loom's evidence directory by path, not by name?",
   "text": "Today any folder called evidence is outside the candidate, so a project's own evidence is unbound unless a witness pins its hashes (failure mode 74). Changing the rule changes the candidate hash of every project that ships an evidence/ folder, including past runs, so it is a versioned decision (loomkit 1.1), not a quiet fix.",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L601",
   "line": 601,
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ],
   "mentions": [
    "fm/74"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "question/15",
   "@type": "OpenQuestion",
   "n": 15,
   "label": "Open question 15: ~~A waiver status (law 43) is new to the Loom.~~ Decided 13 Nov: physics profiles only, for now. The owner is undecided about the concept, and prefers that, if it proves wrong, it is noted here as a false positive rather than deleted. Today's statuses are pass, fail, deferred, not_applicable, blocked and error; the waiver cap lives in the physics witness's coverage and binds no other profile.",
   "headline": "~~A waiver status (law 43) is new to the Loom.~~ Decided 13 Nov: physics profiles only, for now. The owner is undecided about the concept, and prefers that, if it proves wrong, it is noted here as a false positive rather than deleted. Today's statuses are pass, fail, deferred, not_applicable, blocked and error; the waiver cap lives in the physics witness's coverage and binds no other profile.",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L602",
   "line": 602,
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ],
   "mentions": [
    "law/43"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "question/16",
   "@type": "OpenQuestion",
   "n": 16,
   "label": "Open question 16: ~~The three PhysX waivers are reconstructed~~ Answered 13 Nov: the owner owns all three. They were still reconstructed from the marble thread's note (\"user accepted\") by x3d.physics/tools/physx_run_record.py.",
   "headline": "~~The three PhysX waivers are reconstructed~~ Answered 13 Nov: the owner owns all three. They were still reconstructed from the marble thread's note (\"user accepted\") by x3d.physics/tools/physx_run_record.py.",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L603",
   "line": 603,
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "question/17",
   "@type": "OpenQuestion",
   "n": 17,
   "label": "Open question 17: Cross-machine determinism",
   "headline": "Cross-machine determinism",
   "text": "is the one claim every record leaves visible_not_run. Which second machine, and who runs the replay?",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L604",
   "line": 604,
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "question/18",
   "@type": "OpenQuestion",
   "n": 18,
   "label": "Open question 18: MuJoCo has no run record yet",
   "headline": "MuJoCo has no run record yet",
   "text": "Its phase-1 checkpoint replay (mj_getState) is planned; until it lands the physics witness cannot judge a MuJoCo run. Hold the MuJoCo profile until then, or accept a tolerance-style replay row (max_abs_diff against a limit) in loom.physics-run/2?",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L605",
   "line": 605,
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "question/2",
   "@type": "OpenQuestion",
   "n": 2,
   "label": "Open question 2: The IFC bridge fold-back fails its positive control on this Mac",
   "headline": "The IFC bridge fold-back fails its positive control on this Mac",
   "text": "(triangulation differs by platform, §7.4). Fix the witness upstream of promotion (surface comparison), or pin the platform in its profile?",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L589",
   "line": 589,
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "question/3",
   "@type": "OpenQuestion",
   "n": 3,
   "label": "Open question 3: The family pin",
   "headline": "The family pin",
   "text": "Local x3d_mcp is at fa0b389 on fix/physics-findings (17 Oct), not loom-pin-2026-11-01 (decision 5, 1 Nov). Has the tag been created, and should every receipt be re-scored on it [DEF M11]?",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L590",
   "line": 590,
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "question/4",
   "@type": "OpenQuestion",
   "n": 4,
   "label": "Open question 4: The metadata-containerfield warning",
   "headline": "The metadata-containerfield warning",
   "text": "fires on Break-the-Loom controls 09 and 12. Should the projects agent confirm it in X_ITE (is a MetadataSet directly under Shape attached), and if so raise it to an error rule? New evidence (13 Nov, failure mode 141): the MuJoCo bridge's x3d_mcp semantic validator reported it as 5 errors per scene while the XSD passed.",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L591",
   "line": 591,
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ],
   "mentions": [
    "fm/141"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "question/5",
   "@type": "OpenQuestion",
   "n": 5,
   "label": "Open question 5: Ear thresholds",
   "headline": "Ear thresholds",
   "text": "−14 ±1 LUFS (spec) or −18 to −12 (local study, enforced)? v1 keeps both, tied to their profiles, until you choose a production profile.",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L592",
   "line": 592,
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "question/6",
   "@type": "OpenQuestion",
   "n": 6,
   "label": "Open question 6: The C/L/S scale has no \"Contested\" and no \"Question\"",
   "headline": "The C/L/S scale has no \"Contested\" and no \"Question\"",
   "text": "Only the Shroud ledger uses those [DEF §Grades]. Add them to the Loom?",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L593",
   "line": 593,
   "quotedFrom": [
    "doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "question/7",
   "@type": "OpenQuestion",
   "n": 7,
   "label": "Open question 7: Where does stumping's golden-examples log live",
   "headline": "Where does stumping's golden-examples log live",
   "text": ", and should stump runs write Loom receipts [STUMP §Practical playbook]?",
   "definedAt": "https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L594",
